WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.067
David Scheffer.

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.968
He was the first person

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.269
to ever hold that position.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.504
And we also have with us

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.505
the former deputy director

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.640
of National Intelligence, Beth Santer.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:08.708
Thanks to both of you for being here.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:09.442
Really appreciate it.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.744
Let's start with this

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.512
arrest warrant.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.813
Do you think

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.249
it's likely that Putin will actually ever

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.451
stand trial in The Hague

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.453
or face any consequences because of this?

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:21.955
It's possible.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:22.822
And it's possible

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:23.523
because first,

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.592
this is the first step towards

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:28.728
delegitimizing him on a legal scale,

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.864
even before his own people.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.999
Other top leaders who have been indicted,

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.701
whether by the war crimes

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.269
tribunals of the 1990s

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.737
or even by the International

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.772
Criminal Court,

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.307
ultimately lost their authority,

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.842
even domestically.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.343
And they

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.178
then stand the risk of standing

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.480
trial before any of these tribunals

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.915
once that happens.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.183
I don't think we should assume

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.451
that Vladimir Putin

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.352
is in power

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:52.819
for the next

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:55.321
10 to 15 or 20 years in Russia.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.624
At some point, he'll lose that power.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:58.725
And when he does,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.327
I think in part prompted by this

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.363
this arrest warrant against him,

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.330
he'll be subject

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.032
to the possibility of arrest.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:06.800
That's also true.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.701
Even if he travels to India

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.604
or Pakistan or China or North Korea.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.539
It's not that

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.808
he will be immediately arrested,

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.443
but there will be a tremendous

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.343
amount of pressure

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.678
put on those governments,

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.580
particularly India, for example,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.449
not to cater to him,

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.983
because I would suspect

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.318
that some government leaders from

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.252
the G-20

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.022
will actually boycott the G-20 summit

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.457
if if Mr.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.458
Putin indeed

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:32.859
is going to be present there.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.160
They cannot

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.329
as as as was stated in your report,

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.730
they cannot

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.332
literally sit at a table

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.334
and negotiate with an indicted fugitive

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.703
of the International Criminal Court

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.939
or engage in diplomatic discussions

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.108
without a tremendous amount of blowback

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:48.875
if they do so.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:49.542
Do you agree?

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.610
Do you think this will further

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.612
isolate Putin?

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.848
Well, if you look at the autocrats

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.983
that he hangs around with right now,

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.986
none of these people are signatories.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:03.256
So, you know, Iran, North Korea, China

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:04.591
and even these parties

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.725
that are kind of the India

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.727
in-between parties like India.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.395
So, you know, in some ways,

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.330
I think that it almost

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.533
geopolitically solidifies even more

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.367
the divisions

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.902
that we're seeing in our world.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:16.703
You know, countries

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.104
that agree and countries

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.572
that don't agree, even though the U.S.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:20.540
isn't a signatory,

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.975
we support this sort of

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.244
the sort of indictment. Right. Morally.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:25.645
So I do think that there

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.647
is this division, you know,

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.781
but ultimately,

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.317
this just to me reinforces the

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.986
you know, let me count the ways

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.687
of how Putin sees this war

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.489
as an existential war.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.992
Yeah. You know, because if he loses

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:40.860
right
now, you know, the

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.163
consequences are much higher.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.764
So in a way,

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:47.066
this might make him dig in even more.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:47.934
Even though,

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.269
I mean, it's hard to imagine him digging

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:50.069
even in war.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.070
But, you know, historically

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.772
that doesn't really play out.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.907
Once these individuals

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.441
are actually indicted,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.976
it's not as if they're emboldened.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:57.810
They actually start

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.913
to lose their authority

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.281
and their political clout

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:02.115
and they achieve

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:04.284
international pariah status.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.019
This this experience

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:07.754
we experienced this in the 1990s

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.522
and the early 2000s.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.925
Once these leaders are indicted,

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.960
they are not strengthened

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.295
and they don't dig in.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.664
They actually start to draw back.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.399
Although we should note that

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:20.366
Chinese President

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.135
Xi Jinping is traveling to Moscow

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.337
next week to meet with Putin.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.839
Do you think that this could change that

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:27.674
or affect that at all?

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.274
Not at all.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.743
And so so I agree completely with David,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.011
but I also think that, like,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:32.612
we're kind of

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.814
in a different geopolitical moment now

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.182
where, you know,

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.117
what did the foreign ministry of China

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.119
say about this visit coming up?

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:43.423
He he said this is a moment where

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.192
we are two strong powers.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:47.660
We are members, Russia

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.163
and China of the U.N. Security Council.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.331
And this meeting has

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.233
so much more strategic value

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.335
than about our bilateral relationship.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:56.302
This is about

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:59.072
creating an alternative world order.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:02.242
And to me, you know, unfortunately,

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.444
I don't think China is going to be swayed

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.712
by any of this.

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.013
And both of these leaders

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.281
have known for a long time

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.315
that ultimately Mr.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.550
Putin would be indicted.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.685
So it's not as if this is a surprise.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:13.987
They knew this was coming.

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.054
All right, David Scheffer

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:15.688
and Beth Sander,

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:16.889
thanks to both of you for your expertize.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:17.389
Thanks for being here.

